From: Graft64 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: include allocator declarations before CRT definitions

Alloc.cpp defines the C allocation functions but only includes cstdint and
indirect headers. With LLVM-MinGW 20260826 these no longer declare the C
allocation API, leaving C++-linkage definitions and undefined C allocator
symbols when linking libc++ into the ARM64EC module.

Include cstdlib explicitly after clearing the CRT import annotations. Keep
all existing rpmalloc function bodies unchanged. Authored locally from the
native ARM64 CI linker failure; no third-party patch was copied.

Upstream-Status: Pending (not submitted)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/Alloc.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/Alloc.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/Alloc.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/Alloc.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 #define _SECIMP
 #define _CRTIMP
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include "../Priv.h"
 #include <rpmalloc/rpmalloc.h>
 
